py with a route back to the archive and evidence boundary.</p></article></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Thread Outline</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><span class="label">Thread Step</span><h3>Open with the problem: claims spread faster than evidence.</h3><p>Use this copy with a route back to the archive and evidence boundary.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Thread Step</span><h3>Define the archive: maps, books, source lanes, trust boundaries.</h3><p>Use this copy with a route back to the archive and evidence boundary.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Thread Step</span><h3>Explain the rule: association is not guilt.</h3><p>Use this copy with a route back to the archive and evidence boundary.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Thread Step</span><h3>Send readers to the Black File Starter Pack.</h3><p>Use this copy with a route back to the archive and evidence boundary.</p></article></div></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Video Caption</h2><article class="card redline"><h3>A dark archive is useless without source discipline. Start with the Black File, then follow the evidence routes.</h3><p>Caption route should point back to black-file.html.</p></article></section><section class="section wrap"><h2>Downloads</h2><div class="card"><div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="downloads/share-kit-black-file-starter.pdf">PDF Mini Book</a><a class="btn alt" href="downloads/share-kit-black-file-starter.txt">TXT</a><a class="btn alt internal-only" href="downloads/share-kit-black-file-starter.md">Markdown</a><a  class="btn alt machine-data-link internal-only" href="downloads/share-kit-black-file-starter.json">Machine-readable data</a></div></div></section><section id="figure-source-status" class="section wrap source-status-panel"><h2>Figures & Sources</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Figures on this page</span><h3>Checked: 1 July 2026</h3>